{#- Google Analytics (GA4).

    Two guards:

    1. `site.analyticsId` — the measurement ID lives in src/_data/site.json, not
       inline here, so there is one place to change it and no risk of a stale
       copy in a second template.

    2. `runMode == "build"` — `npm run dev` runs Eleventy in "serve" mode, so
       localhost never fires a hit. Without this, every save during a styling
       session lands in the property as real traffic from your own machine, and
       the first week of data is mostly you.

    Alias pages (/their, /seperate, …) deliberately do NOT include this: they
    call location.replace() synchronously, which beats the async gtag load, so
    the hit would be unreliable at best. The canonical page records the visit.
-#}
{%- if site.analyticsId and eleventy.env.runMode == "build" %}
<!-- Google tag (gtag.js) -->
<script async src="https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id={{ site.analyticsId }}"></script>
<script>
  window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];
  function gtag(){dataLayer.push(arguments);}
  gtag('js', new Date());

  gtag('config', '{{ site.analyticsId }}');
</script>
{%- endif %}
